# The other way an overlap is made safe. An exclusive task runs alone, so it is
# never in flight beside the task it shares a path with, and no order between
# them is needed. One side carrying the mark is enough, because the rule that
# holds them apart is symmetric.
run available
exit 0
file tasks/M1-01.md
	---
	id: M1-01
	owns:
	  - crates/normalize
	depends_on: []
	exclusive: yes
	---
file tasks/M1-02.md
	---
	id: M1-02
	owns:
	  - crates/normalize
	depends_on: []
	exclusive: no
	---
stdout
	M1-01
	M1-02
